      <guid isPermaLink="false">69e54860a4ca591452354687</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:43:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from Brussels, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

On today's show, Bloomberg has learnt that the US is set to announce new tariffs on China, the EU and other economies it accuses of hurting American industry. Sources say the additional tariffs won’t lead to an overall rate that exceeds the agreed-upon levels in individual trade deals.

Stocks sold off and Nasdaq 100 futures signaled further weakness as doubts over the durability of the artificial intelligence boom drove investors out of technology shares.

And Jensen Huang has apologized to staff at Nvidia.

Today's guests: Eivind Kallevik, Norsk Hydro, CEO &amp; Fabricio Bloisi, Prosus, CEO. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
